From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: use a 32-aligned stride for linear NV12

With the untiled (linear) primary output, the H616 video engine (H6
variant) reads H.264 reference frames as if the line stride were
32-aligned. Cedrus programmed and exported a 16-aligned stride, so any
width that is a multiple of 16 but not of 32 (720: RG CubeXX 720x720,
RG34XX 720x480, Steam Link's 720x406) decoded the IDR frame correctly
and corrupted every predicted frame (horizontal streaks, green blocks),
with no decode error reported. 640 and 1920 were unaffected.

Use ALIGN(width, 32) for bytesperline, the chroma buffer length and the
VE line stride registers, so userspace and the hardware agree.

Signed-off-by: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -153,8 +153,12 @@
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YVU420:
-		/* 16-aligned stride. */
-		bytesperline = ALIGN(width, 16);
+		/*
+		 * 32-aligned stride: the H6/H616 video engine reads H.264
+		 * reference frames with a 32-aligned stride; a 16-aligned one
+		 * (e.g. 720 wide) corrupts every predicted frame.
+		 */
+		bytesperline = ALIGN(width, 32);
 
 		/* 16-aligned height. */
 		height = ALIGN(height, 16);
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV21:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YUV420:
 	case V4L2_PIX_FMT_YVU420:
-		chroma_size = ALIGN(width, 16) * ALIGN(height, 16) / 2;
+		chroma_size = ALIGN(width, 32) * ALIGN(height, 16) / 2;
 
 		switch (fmt->pixelformat) {
 		case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
@@ -111,8 +111,9 @@
 		reg = chroma_size / 2;
 		cedrus_write(dev, VE_PRIMARY_CHROMA_BUF_LEN, reg);
 
-		reg = VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_LUMA(ALIGN(width, 16)) |
-		      VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA(ALIGN(width, 16) / 2);
+		/* Same 32-aligned stride as cedrus_prepare_format(). */
+		reg = VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_LUMA(ALIGN(width, 32)) |
+		      VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE_CHROMA(ALIGN(width, 32) / 2);
 		cedrus_write(dev, VE_PRIMARY_FB_LINE_STRIDE, reg);
 
 		break;
